(:id "port/python/vt/blobs" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/blobs_test.go: TestPythonVtBlobs, TestPythonVtBlobsNegativeControl/no-shared-refusal" "make python-vt-blobs-negative-control (make/python.mk)") :tested-revision "b449499db7cc1a0dcbdf3cc59c70547de3741df7" :note "2026-11-15: every blobdemo manifest instance (blob_small, blob_empty, blob_large, blob_shared, blob_str8, blob_str16, blob_equal_bytes) loads through the one read and saves back byte-identical with measure equal to length, and blob_shared refuses by name; the run holds both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, built by make dist-python) and the two agree. The negative control drops the shared-blob refusal in a copy of the runtime and the blob_shared row goes red by name. Run on Linux x86-64, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/vt/string-identity" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/blobs_test.go: TestPythonVtBlobs, TestPythonVtBlobsNegativeControl/by-content, TestPythonVtBlobsNegativeControl/by-owner" "make python-vt-blobs-negative-control (make/python.mk)") :tested-revision "b449499db7cc1a0dcbdf3cc59c70547de3741df7" :note "2026-11-15: a caller's equal strings and equal bytes in two blob slots are read from the Go engine's wire, built fresh, and saved BY VALUE, each save byte-identical to the engine's two-record wire, with the caller's values untouched; one *string node named from two slots refuses blob_shared. One table object placed in two by-value slots, and in a by-value slot and a pointer slot, saves byte-identical to the engine's wire of two equal copies, and that save reads back. The by-content control numbers blobs by content in a copy of the save, merging equal slots, and blob_equal_bytes plus the built equal-value rows go red by name; the by-owner control keys a slot's record by the owning table's identity in a copy of the runtime, and both one-object rows go red by name. Run under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, make dist-python) on Linux x86-64, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
